{"title": "Farm-fresh chicken in Jos: pre-order for Christmas 2026", "seo_title": "Farm-Fresh Chicken in Jos: Pre-Order for Christmas 2026 | Colonel Clucks", "description": "Pre-order farm-raised whole or cut chicken in Jos for Christmas 2026. See sizes, how many each bird feeds, pickup and delivery, and how to order. Ready 18 to 23 December.", "content": "<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"lead\"} -->\n<p class=\"lead\">Looking for chicken in Jos for Christmas lunch, a party or a big family table? Batch 1 from our farm is ready 18 to 23 December 2026. This page shows what you can order, what each size feeds and exactly how it works.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"byline\"} -->\n<p class=\"byline\">Written by the <strong>Colonel Clucks team</strong>, Jos, Plateau State · Updated 21 November 2026</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"answer\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group answer\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tag\"} -->\n<p class=\"tag\">The short version</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Chicken for Christmas in Jos: what you need to know</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>What:</strong> farm-raised broilers, whole or cut. You can mix both in one order.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>When:</strong> Batch 1 is ready from 18 to 23 December 2026. You choose your preferred day when you order.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Where:</strong> collect from our farm in Jos, or ask for delivery within Jos.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Sizes:</strong> whole birds in 1.5 kg, 2.5 kg, 3 kg and 3.5 kg sizes. Cut birds pack about 1.5 to 1.9 kg each.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Price:</strong> we are still setting it. We confirm the price when we reply to your order, and no payment is taken on the website.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>How to order:</strong> use our <a href=\"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/#order\">online order form</a> or message us on WhatsApp, +234 913 555 6086.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"toc\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group toc\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"toc-title\"} -->\n<p class=\"toc-title\">On this page</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:list {\"ordered\":true} -->\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#what\">What you can order</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#sizes\">Sizes and how many people each feeds</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#examples\">Example Christmas orders</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#how\">How ordering works</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#collect\">Pickup or delivery</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#choose\">How to choose good chicken in Jos</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#early\">Why order early</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#care\">Storing and cooking</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><a href=\"#faq\">Questions we get asked</a></li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ol>\n<!-- /wp:list --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Products</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"what\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"what\">What you can order</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We sell two things, and only two: <strong>whole birds</strong> and <strong>cut birds</strong>. Both come from our own Batch 1 flock of 50 broilers, which we raise in Jos. On each sale day the birds are prepared fresh in the morning, weighed, labelled and kept chilled until you collect them or we deliver.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cards\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cards\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"card\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group card\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tag\"} -->\n<p class=\"tag\">Whole</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Whole bird</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A whole bird, ready for roasting, boiling or cutting up yourself. Pick a size from 1.5 kg to 3.5 kg.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"card\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group card\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tag\"} -->\n<p class=\"tag\">Cut</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Cut bird</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Cleaned and cut, ready to cook, packed in our Colonel Clucks bag. Each bird is about 1.5 to 1.9 kg.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th></th><th>Whole bird</th><th>Cut bird</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">What you get</th><td>One whole bird, weighed on the day</td><td>One bird, cleaned and cut into pieces, packed in a bag</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Sizes</th><td>1.5 kg, 2.5 kg, 3 kg or 3.5 kg</td><td>About 1.5 to 1.9 kg per bird</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Best for</th><td>Roast chicken on the table, big pots, people who like to cut it themselves</td><td>Jollof and rice meals, stew, pepper soup, peppered chicken, grilling</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Prep at home</th><td>You do the cutting, if you want pieces</td><td>None, it goes straight into the pot or oven</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Can I mix them?</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes, put both numbers in the order form</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Whole or cut: which should you choose?</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tnote\"} -->\n<p class=\"tnote\">Sizes are estimates. We weigh each bird on the sale day and confirm the weight when we confirm your order.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Not sure how much to buy? Our <a href=\"/chicken-size-guide/\">chicken size guide</a> has a calculator and portion tables for families, parties and church or office events.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Sizes</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"sizes\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"sizes\">Sizes and how many people each feeds</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A rule of thumb we use for our own planning: about <strong>450 g of bird per adult</strong> when chicken is the main dish with rice or sides, and about <strong>300 g per adult</strong> at a party with many other dishes. Children usually eat about half. The weights below are the bird weight, bones included.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Whole bird size</th><th>Feeds (main dish, 450 g each)</th><th>Feeds (party, 300 g each)</th><th>Good for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">1.5 kg</th><td>3 adults</td><td>5 adults</td><td>A couple with a guest, or two adults and two children</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">2.5 kg</th><td>5 adults</td><td>8 adults</td><td>A family Christmas lunch</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">3 kg</th><td>6 adults</td><td>10 adults</td><td>A bigger family or a small gathering</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">3.5 kg</th><td>7 adults</td><td>11 adults</td><td>Hungry guests, or a table with leftovers planned</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Whole bird sizes and servings</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tnote\"} -->\n<p class=\"tnote\">Rounded down to whole people. These are planning guides, not a promise of exact weights.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Examples</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"examples\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"examples\">Example Christmas orders</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Here are real-life style examples to copy. They use the portions above, and every total is the bird weight before cooking.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Occasion</th><th>Who is eating</th><th>What to order</th><th>Total bird weight</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Small family lunch</th><td>2 adults and 2 children (about 3 adults of food)</td><td>1 × 1.5 kg whole</td><td>1.5 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Family of six</th><td>6 adults, chicken as the main dish</td><td>1 × 3 kg whole</td><td>3 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Open house</th><td>12 adults, chicken as the main dish</td><td>1 × 3 kg whole + 1 × 2.5 kg whole</td><td>5.5 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Roast plus a pot for the week</th><td>A family that wants a roast on Christmas Day and stew after</td><td>1 × 3 kg whole + 1 cut bird</td><td>About 4.5 to 4.9 kg</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Church or office party</th><td>30 adults, chicken as the main dish</td><td>3 × 3.5 kg whole + 1 × 3 kg whole</td><td>13.5 kg</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Example orders</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"tnote\"} -->\n<p class=\"tnote\">Planning a bigger event, or want a mix we have not listed? Message us on WhatsApp and we will help you work it out.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">How it works</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"how\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how\">How ordering works</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"steps\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group steps\"><!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"step\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group step\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"step-num\"} -->\n<p class=\"step-num\">1</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"step-text\"} -->\n<p class=\"step-text\"><strong>Fill in the order form.</strong> Choose whole or cut, your size, how many birds and your preferred day.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"step\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group step\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"step-num\"} -->\n<p class=\"step-num\">2</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"step-text\"} -->\n<p class=\"step-text\"><strong>Send it to us.</strong> One tap opens WhatsApp or email with your order already written. Nothing is sent until you press send.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"step\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group step\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"step-num\"} -->\n<p class=\"step-num\">3</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"step-text\"} -->\n<p class=\"step-text\"><strong>We confirm.</strong> We reply with availability, the price and how you will pay, then agree pickup or delivery.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n<!-- wp:buttons {\"className\":\"cc-btns\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons cc-btns\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"btn-gold\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button btn-gold\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/#order\">Open the order form</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button -->\n<!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"btn-line\",\"linkTarget\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer noopener\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button btn-line\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://wa.me/2349135556086?text=Hello%20Colonel%20Clucks%2C%20I%20would%20like%20to%20pre-order%20chicken%20for%20Christmas.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Message us on WhatsApp</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>When</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Now to early December</th><td>You send your order. We reply with availability. Final prices are set in early December and we tell everyone who has ordered.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">15 to 17 December</th><td>We confirm every order by WhatsApp and agree your pickup or delivery time.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">18 to 23 December</th><td>Sale days. Birds are prepared fresh each morning, weighed, labelled and kept chilled for collection or delivery.</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">What happens after you order</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"note\"} -->\n<p class=\"note\">Batch 1 is small, so pre-orders are first come, first served. No payment is taken on this website. Price and payment are agreed with you directly.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Getting your chicken</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"collect\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"collect\">Pickup or delivery</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>How it works</th><th>Good to know</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Pickup</th><td>Collect from our farm in Jos on the day we agree.</td><td>We share the pickup details when we confirm your order. Bring a cool bag or a clean cooler if you have a long drive home.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Delivery</th><td>We deliver within Jos. Give us your street, estate or a landmark in the order form.</td><td>Delivery is within Jos only. We confirm any delivery fee when we reply to your order.</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Payment</th><td>Agreed directly with you after we confirm.</td><td>There are no online payments on this website.</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Pickup or delivery compared</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Buyer's checklist</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"choose\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"choose\">How to choose good chicken in Jos</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Whether you buy from us, a market or a shop, these checks help you avoid disappointment. Use them on anyone's chicken, ours included.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:table {\"className\":\"cc-table\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table cc-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Good sign</th><th>Warning sign</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">Smell</th><td>Little or no smell</td><td>A sour, sharp or ammonia smell</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Colour</th><td>Pale pink to cream flesh and skin</td><td>Grey, green or very dark patches</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Feel</th><td>Moist but not sticky, firm flesh that springs back</td><td>A slimy or tacky film, soft flesh</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Temperature</th><td>Cold to the touch, kept on ice or in a fridge</td><td>Left in the sun or at room temperature for hours</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Weight</th><td>Weighed on a scale in front of you</td><td>A guessed weight or no scale</td></tr></tbody></table><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">What to check before you buy raw chicken</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Questions to ask any seller</h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>When was this bird prepared, and how has it been kept since?</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Is the price per bird or per kilogram?</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Can I see the weight on the scale?</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li>Can I see where the birds were raised, or photos and video of the farm?</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We are happy to answer all four. You can see how we raise our birds on the <a href=\"/about-the-farm/\">our farm page</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Planning</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"early\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"early\">Why order early</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Christmas is the busiest time of year for chicken in Nigeria. Newspapers report each December that prices rise and supplies tighten, and this season industry reporting also mentions a shortage of day-old chicks. You can read more at <a href=\"https://nairametrics.com/2025/12/02/prices-of-chicken-surge-what-families-should-expect-this-christmas\" rel=\"noopener\">Nairametrics</a> and <a href=\"https://live.poultryworld.net/the-industrymarkets/market-trends-analysis-the-industrymarkets-2/day-old-chick-shortage-puts-nigerian-poultry-farmers-under-pressure-ahead-of-christmas/\" rel=\"noopener\">Poultry World</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>For us the reason is simpler. Batch 1 is 50 birds. When they are spoken for, they are gone, and a pre-order lets you pick your size and your day before the rush.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">At home</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"care\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"care\">Storing and cooking your chicken</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\"><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Keep it cold.</strong> Put raw chicken in the fridge (4°C or colder) as soon as you get home and cook it within 2 days. Freeze it the same day if you cannot.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Cook it through.</strong> Chicken is safe when the thickest part of the thigh reaches at least 74°C (165°F) and the juices run clear. See <a href=\"https://chautauqua.cce.cornell.edu/food-nutrition/food-safety-storage/safe-minimum-cooking-temperatures\" rel=\"noopener\">Cornell Cooperative Extension</a>.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --><!-- wp:list-item -->\n<li><strong>Keep raw and cooked apart.</strong> Use a separate board and knife for raw chicken, and wash your hands after touching it.</li>\n<!-- /wp:list-item --></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Roasting times for each size, thawing times and leftovers advice are in our <a href=\"/chicken-size-guide/#cook\">size guide</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">FAQ</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading {\"anchor\":\"faq\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"faq\">Questions we get asked</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Do you sell live birds?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>No. We sell <strong>whole birds</strong> and <strong>cut birds</strong> only, prepared fresh on the sale day.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>When can I get my chicken?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Batch 1 is ready from <strong>18 to 23 December 2026</strong>. Pick your preferred day in the order form. We confirm every order by WhatsApp between 15 and 17 December.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>How much does it cost?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We have not set the final price yet, because we are still checking costs and the Jos market. We confirm the price when we reply to your order, and we will not take payment before then.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Can I pay on the website?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>No. The website only sends your order to us on WhatsApp or by email. We agree price and payment with you directly.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Do you deliver outside Jos?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Not for Batch 1. We deliver within Jos, or you can collect from the farm.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Is the chicken fresh or frozen?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Fresh. We prepare the birds in the morning on the sale days and keep them chilled until you collect or we deliver. If you need to keep your chicken longer than 2 days, freeze it the day you get it.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>Can I mix whole and cut birds in one order?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Yes. Put the number of whole birds and the number of cut birds in the order form, for example 3 whole and 2 cut.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>How big are the birds?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>We offer whole birds in 1.5 kg, 2.5 kg, 3 kg and 3.5 kg sizes, and cut birds of about 1.5 to 1.9 kg. We weigh every bird on the sale day and confirm the weight.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details -->\n<!-- wp:details -->\n<details class=\"wp-block-details\"><summary>What if I need chicken for a big event?</summary>\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Message us on <a href=\"https://wa.me/2349135556086?text=Hello%20Colonel%20Clucks%2C%20I%20need%20chicken%20for%20an%20event.\" rel=\"noopener\">WhatsApp</a> with your date and number of guests. Batch 1 is small, so the earlier you ask, the better.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></details>\n<!-- /wp:details --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Who wrote this</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This page was written by the Colonel Clucks team. We are a small farm-raised start-up in Jos, Plateau State, raising Batch 1 of 50 broilers in collaboration with Longon Farms Nigeria Limited. We share what we do on our <a href=\"/about-the-farm/\">farm page</a> and on <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/colonelclucks/\" rel=\"noopener\">Instagram</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"disclose\"} -->\n<p class=\"disclose\"><strong>Full disclosure:</strong> we sell the chicken described on this page, so we have a commercial interest. The portion and storage advice is general guidance that applies to any chicken. Sizes and dates are our current plan and we update this page when anything changes.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"cc-section\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group cc-section\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"eyebrow\"} -->\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">Keep reading</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">More from the farm</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"related\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group related\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"rel\"} -->\n<p class=\"rel\"><a href=\"/chicken-size-guide/\"><strong>How much chicken per person?</strong></a><br>A calculator, portion tables and cooking times.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"className\":\"rel\"} -->\n<p class=\"rel\"><a href=\"/about-the-farm/\"><strong>Inside our farm</strong></a><br>Our daily routine, feed plan and Batch 1 facts.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"className\":\"ctaband\",\"align\":\"full\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group ctaband alignfull\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":{{IMG_HAPPY}}_ID,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"className\":\"cta-mascot\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full cta-mascot\"><img src=\"{{IMG_HAPPY}}_URL\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-{{IMG_HAPPY}}_ID\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ready to reserve your birds?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Batch 1 is ready 18 to 23 December 2026. Order now and pick your size and your day.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n<!-- wp:buttons {\"className\":\"cc-btns\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons cc-btns\"><!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"btn-gold\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button btn-gold\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/#order\">Place your order</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button -->\n<!-- wp:button {\"className\":\"btn-line\",\"linkTarget\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"noreferrer noopener\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-button btn-line\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"https://wa.me/2349135556086?text=Hello%20Colonel%20Clucks%2C%20I%20have%20a%20question%20about%20ordering%20chicken.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Ask on WhatsApp</a></div>\n<!-- /wp:button --></div>\n<!-- /wp:buttons --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:html -->\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"Article\", \"headline\": \"Farm-fresh chicken in Jos: pre-order for Christmas 2026\", \"description\": \"Pre-order farm-raised whole or cut chicken in Jos for Christmas 2026. See sizes, how many each bird feeds, pickup and delivery, and how to order. Ready 18 to 23 December.\", \"datePublished\": \"2026-11-21\", \"dateModified\": \"2026-11-21\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/christmas-chicken-jos.html\", \"image\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/logo.png\", \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Colonel Clucks Poultry\", \"url\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/\"}, \"publisher\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Colonel Clucks Poultry\", \"logo\": {\"@type\": \"ImageObject\", \"url\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/logo.png\"}}}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Christmas chicken in Jos\", \"item\": \"https://colonelclucks.netlify.app/christmas-chicken-jos.html\"}]}</script>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "slug": "christmas-chicken-jos"}